== Trivia ==
* The achievement for unlocking Tainted Eden is "The Capricious", a possible name for the character.
** "Capricious" means "given to sudden and unaccountable changes of mood or behavior," fitting Tainted Eden's concept of complete randomness.
* Tainted Eden's hairstyle will change every time they are hit.
* On the stage transition screen, their body glitches in a unique animation. Prior to [[V1.7.5|Version 1.7.5]], their portrait did not appear whatsoever.
** This animation features snippets of other portraits from different characters and bosses. These include {{E|Monstro}}, {{c|Dead Tainted Lazarus}}, {{c|The Forgotten}}, {{c|Apollyon}}, {{E|The Bloat}}, and {{c|Isaac}}, but colored and shaded to resemble how he appeared in the Flash version of The Binding of Isaac.
* Tainted Eden's starting stats are listed as "?" on the character selection screen.
* In-development, Tainted Eden's effect was a full reroll upon acquiring a new item that excluded the item triggering the reroll rather than having the reroll be triggered by damage. This was changed because in testing players would simply stop picking up items once they found something good enough to be worth keeping.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/123641386921754625/485133685881045014/847218561746993163 Conversation from Kilburn via the Binding of Isaac Community Discord</ref><ref>https://i.imgur.com/06ms8k5.png Imgur mirror</ref>
* Oddly enough, Tainted Eden unlocks {{P|XXI - The World?}}, associated with stagnation and inertia, this in relation of unfinished goals, lack of motivation and roadblocks, as any builds Tainted Eden makes will be lost in a hit, causing runs to feel meaningless and take free hits hoping for a better build or require absolute perfection to keep a strong build.

== Bugs ==
{{bug|If Tainted Eden is firing {{i|Technology 2}} when damage triggers a re-roll, sometimes the laser persists firing in the last-fired direction until leaving the room, even picking up new synergies as other items reroll.}}
{{bug|If the active item is re-rolled into {{I|Alabaster Box}} it will be fully charged instead of discharged as usual.}}
{{Bug|If Tainted Eden first looks at an item on a floor (such as treasure room items, shop items, golden chest item drops, etc), but does not take them until after walking into a new room with an item in it (such as a Devil/Angel room), those items will be re-rolled into items of the pool most recently walked into.}}
{{bug|If Tainted Eden rerolls into modded items that must be unlocked to be acquired, and they are not unlocked, the item will be rerolled into nothing, and an item will be lost. This can also cause crashes.}}

